@startuml block_loop
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam ArrowFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor #273241
 BorderColor #61738a
 FontColor #e6edf7
}
skinparam note {
 BackgroundColor #1b2533
 BorderColor #61738a
 FontColor #e6edf7
}
title L2_AUDIO block loop: one iteration per 4 ms block (design, not implemented)
start
:Start command from L2_CONTROL;
:i2s_start\nprime 4 silent TX blocks, start RX, then TX;
:started event to L2_CONTROL;
repeat
  :**WAIT** i2s_receiveBlock\nwaits for the next completed RX block, at most 20 ms (P11); <<#345E87>>
  if (result) then (timeout or driver error)
    :microphone failure;
    (F)
    detach
  else (OK: RX block lent)
  endif
  :take the left slot (even index) of each of the 64 frames\ninto the 64-entry mono working buffer (low 8 bits cleared);
  :**i2s_releaseReceivedBlock**\nRX block back to the RX pool;
  :process the mono buffer\nthis step: copy; later listening filter and volume;
note right
  Processing budget (P02): from the received block
  to the queued TX block at most 3 ms of the 4 ms period;
  the receive wait is not part of it.
  No lock is held across a block wait.
  The thread holds at most one RX and one TX block:
  RX is returned before TX is requested.
end note
  :**WAIT** i2s_allocateTransmitBlock\nwaits for a free TX block, at most 20 ms (P11); <<#345E87>>
  if (result) then (timeout)
    :output failure;
    (F)
    detach
  else (OK: TX block held)
  endif
  :write each mono sample into both slots of its frame;
  :**i2s_transmitBlock**\nownership passes to the driver;
  if (result) then (failure)
    :L1_I2S returns the block to the TX pool,\nthen output failure;
    (F)
    detach
  else (OK)
  endif
  :**STOP CHECK** command queue, without waiting; <<#4a3a1a>>
repeat while (Stop received?) is (no)
->yes;
:i2s_stop (see Stop sequence);
:stopped event to L2_CONTROL;
stop
partition "Fault exit, reached from every (F)" {
(F)
:i2s_abort: DROP on both links at once;
:fault event with the failed link to L2_CONTROL;
:wait for commands; restart required;
stop
}
@enduml
